    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d519">

                <pb facs="1349" n="1333" sameAs="frus:frus1951v01/pg1333"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">394.31/1–2951: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in France</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Bonsai</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Paris</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1951-01-29T19:00:00+01:00">January 29, 1951—7
                            p. m</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>4461. Torquay’s telegram 370, January 26, 1951 to Washington, repeated Paris 26,
                    January 26, 1951.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d519-f1"/> Embassy office took occasion
                    ask Wormser,<anchor n="2" xml:id="d519-f2"/> in charge multilateral affairs,
                        FonOff views re French position
                    Blankenstein tariff reduction proposal. Wormser confidentially indicated that
                        FonOff was definitely opposed. Embassy
                    suggests that statement by Lecuyer<anchor n="3" xml:id="d519-f3"/> supporting
                    further exploration Blankenstein proposal should be interpreted
                        accordingly.<anchor n="4" xml:id="d519-f4"/>
                </p>
                <p>Sent Department 4461, repeated information Torquay 16.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bonsal</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d519-f1" n="1" xml:id="d519-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d519-f2" n="2" xml:id="d519-f2-content">
                <p>Olivier Wormser, <hi rendition="#italic">Chef de Service</hi>, Economic
                    Cooperation, in Economic and Financial Affairs, French Ministry of Foreign
                    Affairs.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d519-f3" n="3" xml:id="d519-f3-content">
                <p>Ernest Lecuyer, member of the French Delegation to the Torquay Conference.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d519-f4" n="4" xml:id="d519-f4-content">
                <p>Lecuyer’s statement had been reported in telegram 370, January 26, not
                    printed.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
